    "body": "Triage, checked on `main` 8f30bee:\n\n**Setup sheets and the tool list exist, but a new document can't reach them.** Both are on the **Setups** page: the tool list (per tool: ops, changes, cut and rapid length, estimated minutes), and **Export setup sheets...**, which writes one text page per setup. Post doesn't write them; the README's \"print alongside\" is wrong about that. The bug the reporter hit is how to get to that page:\n- The only way in is the browser's **Setups** row (`panes::browser_rows`), and that row is drawn only once the document has a named setup (`setup::names` non-empty).\n- A new document has no named setup (the global stock and G54-G59 act as the first one), so the row isn't there. The page itself handles that case (\"No setups in this document ... Create first setup\", plus the tool list and the export button), but nothing navigates to it.\n- That's the open part of #45 (\"expose the Setups page in a new document\"). Drawing the row always would fix it, but it changes the default browser, so the shell pixel snapshots move, and those can only be regenerated on the CI platform (#255).\n\n**README:** it lists Fanuc, Haas, Mazak, Sinumerik, Heidenhain and Fanuc Lathe, but not the **Tormach PathPilot** post (`assets/posts/tormach.cps`, #131) or the Tormach machines (770MX, 770MX (ML), 770M, 1100MX, 1500MX, PCNC 440).\n\n**Help -> About:** there's no About entry anywhere in the UI (no \"About\" string in `crates/ui`). That's a separate, small enhancement if wanted.\n\n\nclaimed: austin62jake (Claude Code agent) · 2026-11-08T14:43Z · branch issue/267-readme-posts · plan: README only - name the Tormach PathPilot post and the shipped Tormach machines, and say the setup sheet and tool list come from the Setups page (Export setup sheets...), not from Post. `Refs`, not `Fixes`: making the Setups page reachable in a new document stays with #45.\n",
